# Exclude reports/ by default, but the API reads a handful of these CSVs at
# request time -- keep exactly those (interval calibration/coverage
# diagnostics, both targets' dynamic ensemble weight sources, and the backtest
# predictions /rba-action reads). Use reports/* (not a bare "reports") so the
# negations below actually take effect; Docker cannot un-exclude files inside a
# wholesale-ignored parent directory. When an endpoint starts reading a new
# report, add it here, or the deployed image will 503 on that endpoint while
# everything works locally.
reports/*
!reports/model_interval_coverage.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_factors.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_validation.csv
!reports/model_interval_coverage_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_factors_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/model_interval_calibration_validation_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/model_comparison_elastic_net.csv
!reports/model_comparison_elastic_net_trimmed_mean.csv
!reports/backtest_predictions.csv
!reports/backtest_predictions_trimmed_mean.csv
